# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  bel-angst — no envs are read by the browser.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# In Azure mode, bel-angst calls /api/realtime-token and /api/chat
# (same-origin). Those Functions read their keys from Application
# Settings on the Static Web App. See ../api/local.settings.json.example
# for the local-dev shape. Relevant envs on the server side:
#
#   AZURE_REALTIME_ENDPOINT     https://<your-realtime>.openai.azure.com
#   AZURE_REALTIME_API_KEY      server-side only, never in the browser
#   AZURE_REALTIME_DEPLOYMENT   e.g. gpt-4o-realtime
#   AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT       https://<your-chat>.openai.azure.com
#   AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY        server-side only
#   AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT     e.g. gpt-4o-mini
#
# In "OpenAI direct" mode the user pastes their own sk-... key into the
# UI — it lives in localStorage and is sent straight to api.openai.com.
